      "timed": {
        "claims": "As electrical.",
        "omissions": []
      },
      "electrical": {
        "claims": "Two op-amps (SPEC-004 opamp) at the datasheet's typical open-loop gain, a single pole at its gain-bandwidth, its slew rate, and its output swing from each rail; fixtures on +/-15 V for a follower, the positive and negative swing, the slew rate and the bandwidth from those values.",
        "omissions": [
          "input offset voltage, bias and offset currents (picoamperes, doubling every 10 C), and their drift",
          "the common-mode input range: the classic TL072 inverts its output when an input comes within about 2 V of the negative rail (phase reversal); not modelled nor diagnosed",
          "further poles, the phase margin and the capacitive-load stability",
          "the output short-circuit current (about 26 mA) and the swing's dependence on the load",
          "noise (37 nV/rtHz)",
          "supply current (1.4 mA per channel)",
          "temperature dependence",
          "device-to-device spread"
        ],
        "validation": [
          "tests/*.json"
        ]
      }
    },
